      "source": "https://indianvillagefw.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Indian Village is listed on the National Register of Historic Places, the nation’s official list of properties considered worthy of preservation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://indianvillagefw.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nearly 500 homes span architectural styles from Tudor Revival and Spanish Colonial to Mid-Century Modern ranch homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://indianvillagefw.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Many streets in Indian Village are named after characters from Longfellow’s epic poem 'Song of Hiawatha'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
