      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Before becoming a subdivision, the land that is now Indian Village housed the Allen County Farm for the Poor and an orphanage since 1864.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://indianvillagefw.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The original brochure proclaimed Indian Village the greatest real estate enterprise in Fort Wayne, covering 200 acres and seven miles of wide boulevards.",
